PKG=zeth46
NAME=z3660eth-k46 1.0.0-13 - Z3660 ethernet driver module, k46 line
ARCH=Amiga
VERSION=1.0.0-13
CATEGORY=system
CLASSES=none z3660eth
VENDOR=amix
PSTAMP=amix-zeth46-1.0.0-13
# Kernel space (amix-dlm C2-2, C3-5 sec 1): a role=module entry of the
# #ext kpkg block (line=k46), never an ordinary entry.  Catalog name
# z3660eth-k46, pkginst zeth46.  The module's release is
# kernel/drivers/z3660eth/module/VERSION (1.0.0-7), the same on both lines;
# 1.0.0-13 is a package revision of it.  The node is in class z3660eth
# (C3-5 sec 1.2).
APKG_DESC=Z3660 onboard ethernet (zen0, STREAMS/DLPI) as a boot-class kernel module for the 68040/68060 line module kernel kernel-k46-m: /etc/conf/mod.d/z3660eth, /dev/zen0 and the link.d entry ifup reads (/etc/inet/link.d/z3660eth).
DESC=The kernel/drivers/z3660eth driver built as an amix-dlm kernel module for the 68040/68060 line: boot class, loaded at the first sysinit entry (modadmin -B) when a Z3660 is present (match zorro:144b:01, mobo:z3660-window), character major 51, its node /dev/zen0 (c 51 0, mode 0600) shipped by the package.  /etc/inet/link.d/z3660eth (zen /dev/zen 0 51) tells ifup the interface prefix, the node, the first unit and the major; configure zen0 in /etc/inet/interfaces, not there.  /etc/conf/modreg.d/z3660eth holds the package's defaults (none).  The package writes no boot store; after the install apkg runs kbootset build and commit (or prints the command when bootset=manual).  MIT.
